<Popup Visible="@Visible" VisibleChanged="@OnVisibleChamged" Title="Medicine Help">
    <h2>Medicines</h2>
    <p>
        Medicines is where you can keep track of the medicines you are prescribed to help with your health problems. You can keep track
        of your dose, who and when they were prescribed, and your schedule for taking them. Changes in the medicines are logged to help you 
        build a profile of the medicines you have taken over time.
    </p>
    <h2>Medicine Reports</h2>
    <p>
        Medicine reports largely exist to confirm that you have taken your medicine at the schedule you provided. You will be reminded
        to create a medicine report every time you are due to take your medicine, this lets you keep track of what medicine you took and
        when you took it.n
    </p>
    <p>
        Reports can be created for medicines either by pressing the <span class="material-symbols-outlined">article</span> button next to the
        medicine like symptoms, or if you have been due to take your medicine since filling in the last medicine report you will be reminded
        on the home screen that the medicine report is due.
    </p>
</Popup>

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool Visible { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> VisibleChanged { get; set; }

    private async Task OnVisibleChamged(bool visible)
    {
        await VisibleChanged.InvokeAsync(visible);
    }
}
